@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@token = REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_AUTHENTICATED_BEARER_TOKEN
@tenantId = REPLACE_WITH_INTERNAL_ORGANIZATION_ID
@personId = REPLACE_WITH_PERSON_ID_FROM_CONTACT_RESPONSE
@directoryTenantId = REPLACE_WITH_MEMBER_TOKEN_TID
@objectId = REPLACE_WITH_MEMBER_TOKEN_OID
@membershipId = REPLACE_WITH_MEMBERSHIP_ID_FROM_GRANT_RESPONSE

### Create an isolation organization without inventing a directory mapping.
### This remains Pending onboarding; it creates neither memberships nor administrator roles.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"displayName":"Local test organization"}

### Public login bootstrap: no tenant or membership required
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login-config

### Discover contexts without choosing a browser-global active organization
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/workspaces?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Explicit organization request; homeTenant can be null
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### CSP operator: find an existing organization-local Person (contact email grants no access)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/membership-persons?query=
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### CSP operator: create contact if none exists; creates neither membership nor role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/membership-persons
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"displayName":"Local test member","email":"local-member@example.invalid"}

### CSP or existing organization Administrator: explicit trusted identity association
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"directoryTenantId":"{{directoryTenantId}}","objectId":"{{objectId}}","personId":"{{personId}}"}

### List active and revoked grants (CSP context); org admins instead send their organization headers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Read the resource referenced by a successful grant's Location header
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Revoke; last accessible organization Administrator returns 409 LAST_ADMIN_PROTECTED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Support entry is separately audited and never creates ordinary membership
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/impersonate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Use the response's HttpOnly cookie through your local HTTP client's cookie jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: support

### Exit support using CSP scope, including when the support token has expired
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tenants/impersonation
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: csp
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Negative test: unknown or revoked membership returns 403, never a home-tenant fallback
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
